Event Registration Formatter

Description
This Python program collects student information and event details. It uses string methods to clean and format text inputs and the datetime module to display the event date in a readable format.

Features
- Accepts the student's first and last name.
- Formats the full name using title case.
- Converts the full name and section into uppercase.
- Cleans the event name using string methods.
- Displays the event date in a readable format.
- Uses Python's datetime module.

Language Used
- Python

String Methods Used
- "strip()" – Removes unnecessary spaces.
- "title()" – Capitalizes the first letter of each word.
- "upper()" – Converts text into uppercase.

Date/Time Feature Used
- "datetime" – Creates and formats the event date.

Versions
1. Version 1 – Basic input and output.
2. Version 2 – Added string formatting methods.
3. Version 3 – Added date formatting using datetime.

How to Run
1. Open the Python source code file.
2. Run the program.
3. Enter the requested student and event information.
4. View the formatted registration summary.
